  Your ask — "notified when tasks they care about change" — lands in 2 and 3. Neither can be specified honestly until 1
  exists, because a reminder rule is a predicate over a task schema that doesn't have fields yet.

  One thing genuinely upstream of all of it, though: [1mwhere a reminder is allowed to reach you.[0m An in-app badge needs
  nothing. A browser notification that fires while the tab is closed needs a service worker and a permission prompt.
  Email or phone push needs a server and an address for every user — which would put a backend into sub-project 1, not
  3, and would undo the "stays in the browser" assumption we just made.
